					"text": "tap.python.spike-q2-outlets\n\nQ2 (M1): outlet_insert_after between the box's dynlet_begin and dynlet_end puts a new outlet before the dumpout, and the cords of the outlets that stay survive; outlet_delete removes the right one. 'describe' lists outlet_nth against what the object holds and every cord from the box; 'fire' outputs each value outlet's number (q2-outlet-N) and 'fired' from the dumpout (q2-dumpout). After 'outlets 3' the new outlet 2 is cord-ed to q2-new by scripting.",
